    "area": "Canyonlands, Island in the Sky",
    "signature": "The switchbacks off the mesa, in full view of anyone at the top.",
    "summary": "The Shafer Trail drops off the Island in the Sky in a stack of exposed switchbacks to the White Rim. You can see the whole descent from the overlook before you commit.",
    "why": "It is the moment the park stops being a scenic drive.",
    "highlights": [
      "The switchbacks",
      "The junction with the White Rim and Potash Road"
    ],
    "best": "March–November, if the rock is dry",
    "time": "19 miles · 1–2 hours for the descent itself",
    "difficulty": "High clearance. The shelf is the difficulty, not the rocks. A nervous passenger will not enjoy it. Turn around at the top if you are unsure.",
    "elevation": "From about 6,000 ft on the mesa to the bench",
    "fee": "Canyonlands entrance.",
    "access": "From the Island in the Sky road, signed Shafer. The top has an overlook. Use it.",
    "tips": [
      "Walk the first switchback with your eyes before you drive it.",
      "Uphill traffic and bikes share the shelf. The outside tire is the one that matters."
    ],
