    "lat": 38.59498,
    "lng": -109.54474,
    "area": "Sand Flats, above Moab",
    "signature": "The slickrock loop you can see from town.",
    "summary": "Hell's Revenge is the Sand Flats slickrock trail on the bench above Moab: domes, ledges, and a loop that the whole town can watch. It is a real rock trail, with bypasses for the famous obstacles and no bypass for bad judgment.",
    "why": "It is the trail that defines Moab, which means it is crowded and still worth doing once, correctly.",
    "highlights": [
      "The main loop",
      "The optional obstacles, which are optional",
      "The view of the La Sals and the valley"
    ],
    "best": "March–May and September–November. Summer slickrock burns skin and tires. Closed at night in places.",
    "time": "7.2 miles · 3–5 hours",
    "difficulty": "Modified. Rock crawler for the obstacles. High-clearance 4x4 with a locker can use the bypasses and still have a day.",
    "elevation": "About 4,500–4,800 ft on the slickrock",
    "fee": "Sand Flats Recreation Area fee. Pay at the entrance.",
    "permit": "Daylight hours. The area is busy. Stay on the marked trail. The slickrock next to it is not a shortcut.",
    "access": "Sand Flats entrance on the east side of Moab, up Sand Flats Road.",
    "tips": [
      "Walk the hard lines before you drive them.",
      "One vehicle at a time on the obstacles. The person behind you is not your spotter unless you asked."
    ],
    "watch": "Slickrock punishes a wrong tire. Heat, crowds, and people riding onto the line you are crawling.",
    "status": "Sand Flats fee. Check if an obstacle is one-way or bypassed.",
