    "area": "Grand Staircase-Escalante, between Cannonville and US-89",
    "signature": "The dirt highway through the monument.",
    "summary": "Cottonwood Canyon Road crosses Grand Staircase-Escalante from near Cannonville and Kodachrome to US-89. It is a long, scenic, usually-maintained dirt road through the Cockscomb and the Cottonwood narrows. When it is wet it is a 4x4 road, which the signs say because they have to.",
    "why": "The one road that explains the monument, if the road is open.",
    "highlights": [
      "The Cockscomb",
      "Cottonwood Narrows",
      "Grosvenor Arch, off a spur"
    ],
    "best": "Spring and fall. Closed or foolish when wet. Summer is hot in the narrows.",
    "time": "43 miles · Half a day to a full day",
    "difficulty": "High clearance recommended. Often passable to a careful SUV when dry and recently graded. Not when wet.",
    "elevation": "About 5,000–6,500 ft",
    "fee": "Grand Staircase-Escalante. Grosvenor Arch is a side road. Stay on the road.",
    "access": "From Cannonville near Kodachrome Basin, or from US-89 west of Page. Check which end is open.",
