    "lng": -112.11973,
    "area": "Grand Staircase, between Cannonville and Bull Valley Gorge",
    "signature": "A narrower monument road, with a gorge you do not joke about.",
    "summary": "Skutumpah Road runs from near Cannonville toward Johnson Canyon and US-89, past Bull Valley Gorge, where a pickup has been lodged in the slot since 1954. The road is high clearance and more serious than Cottonwood when it is rough.",
    "why": "The gorge is the story. The road is how you earn it.",
    "highlights": [
      "Bull Valley Gorge",
      "The Willis Creek area",
      "The long grade toward Kanab"
    ],
    "best": "Spring and fall. Mud closes it in practice.",
    "time": "20 miles · Most of a day",
    "difficulty": "High clearance. Narrow. Some ledges. Not a rock trail, not a sedan.",
    "elevation": "About 6,000 ft",
    "fee": "Grand Staircase-Escalante.",
    "access": "From Cannonville, or from the Johnson Canyon side. Willis Creek is a popular hike off the road.",
    "tips": [
      "Look at the gorge from the bridge and do not climb into the slot for the truck.",
      "The road is slower than the mileage."
    ],
    "watch": "A narrow shelf and a gorge that has already collected one truck.",
