    "best": "Year-round when dry. Mud and snow on the high end.",
    "time": "15 miles · 2–4 hours",
    "difficulty": "High clearance recommended. Not a rock trail. Rough if it has not been graded.",
    "elevation": "From the high country down to the river",
    "fee": "National forest and private ranch land. The road is public. The ranch is not. Stay on the road.",
    "access": "From Jerome / Perkinsville, or from the Chino Valley side.",
    "tips": [
      "Cattle and horses have the right of way because they do not care about yours.",
      "The river crossing, if you meet one, gets looked at on foot."
    ],
    "watch": "Rough gravel and private land on both sides.",
