    "signature": "A 4x4 road up a fourteener, which is a bad idea to misunderstand.",
    "summary": "The Mount Antero road is a mining road that climbs high on a 14,000-foot peak west of Buena Vista, famous among rock hounds and among people who underestimate a fourteener. The road is rough, high, and optional. The summit is a hike from wherever you wisely stop.",
