    "area": "Mogollon Mountains, NM-159",
    "signature": "The narrow mountain road over the Mogollon crest.",
    "summary": "Bursum Road, NM-159, climbs from the Glenwood side over the Mogollon Mountains toward Mogollon ghost town and the high crest. It is a narrow, cliff-cut forest highway, paved in stretches and raw in others, with no guardrail where you most want one.",
    "why": "The Gila's great road, and the reason people in Glenwood give you a look when you say you are going up.",
    "highlights": [
      "The shelf above the canyons",
      "Mogollon, if you take the spur",
      "The crest of the Mogollon Mountains"
    ],
    "best": "May–October. Snow closes the top. Monsoon rockfall happens.",
    "time": "32 miles · Half a day",
    "difficulty": "Usually a careful car. Very narrow and exposed. Not a rock-crawler trail. Trailers and large RVs should not.",
