    "lat": 33.31732,
    "lng": -108.83391,
    "area": "Gila, near the Catwalk",
    "signature": "The canyon road to the Catwalk.",
    "summary": "Whitewater Road runs up the canyon to the Catwalk National Recreation Trail, where a metal walkway hangs on the wall of a slot. The road is the way to a short, astonishing walk. The canyon above is forest and wilderness, not a continuation for your vehicle.",
    "why": "A drive that ends at a trail, which is the correct ending.",
    "highlights": [
      "The Catwalk",
      "The canyon"
    ],
    "best": "March–November. The Catwalk has been rebuilt after floods and can close. Check.",
    "time": "2.2 miles · 2–3 hours with the walk",
    "difficulty": "Usually a careful car to the trailhead. The side roads are rougher.",
    "elevation": "About 5,000–6,000 ft",
    "fee": "National forest recreation site. A day fee may apply at the Catwalk.",
    "access": "From Glenwood, up Whitewater Canyon.",
    "tips": [
      "Check that the Catwalk is open. Floods close it.",
      "The wilderness above the trailhead is not a jeep road."
    ],
    "watch": "Flash floods in the canyon. Do not drive up it under a storm.",
    "status": "The Catwalk can close after floods.",
