    "area": "Moapa Valley, north of Lake Mead",
    "signature": "The valley's main OHV network, named like a playlist.",
    "summary": "Logandale Trails is the BLM open area above the Moapa Valley: a mapped stack of loops, from the main loop to rock-crawler lines with names like Jack's Reward and Sidewinder. The lines on this map are the named trails, not the whole desert.",
    "why": "If you want a system, with trail names and a way back to the trailer, this is the one near Las Vegas.",
    "highlights": [
      "Trail 1, the main loop",
      "Jackrabbit and Lookout",
      "The harder named lines, if the machine matches the trail"
    ],
    "best": "October–April. Midsummer is for people who misread the forecast.",
    "time": "27 miles · Half a day to a full day",
    "difficulty": "Mixed. The main loop is high clearance and side-by-sides. Named rock trails are modified.",
    "elevation": "About 1,500–2,500 ft",
    "fee": "BLM Logandale Trails. Free to ride the designated trails. Stay in the system. The Muddy River valley below is not part of the playground.",
